---
import Biz from '../../components/Biz.astro';
import Prose from '../../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { siteData } from '../../lib/site';

const { business: b } = await siteData();
---

<Prose
  title={`Terms of service | ${b.brandName}`}
  description="The terms for using OSuite, buying a subscription and using osuite.business."
  lines={['Terms of', 'service']}
  standfirst="The agreement between you and us when you use OSuite or buy a plan."
  meta="Last updated 15 October 2026"
>
  <h2>The agreement</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are between you (the business using OSuite) and <Biz k="legalName" fallback="OfinIT" />. By installing OSuite, starting a trial or
    buying a plan you accept them, together with the <a href="/legal/eula">licence agreement</a>, the <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a>
    and the <a href="/legal/refunds">refund policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A plan gives the number of users shown on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>, for the period you pay for, monthly or yearly.</li>
    <li>Prices are in Indian rupees. <span data-biz="gstNote">{b.gstNote || 'Prices exclude 18% GST'}</span>; we issue a GST tax invoice for every payment.</li>
    <li>Plans renew only when you pay for the next period. If a period ends unpaid, OSuite gives 7 days’ grace and then turns read-only.</li>
    <li>We may change prices for future periods; a change never applies to a period already paid for, and we tell you at least 30 days ahead.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    Your business data belongs to you. On the desktop edition it stays on your computer, and you are responsible for keeping backups; OSuite helps
    with daily backups and copies to a second folder. With cloud hosting we keep your data and backups on your behalf and return them on request.
  </p>

  <h2>Tax and accounting</h2>
  <p>
    OSuite calculates GST and prepares returns from what you enter. You remain responsible for your tax filings and the accuracy of your entries;
    please have your accountant review your returns. E-invoicing through the government portal depends on the portal and on our GST Suvidha
    Provider being available.
  </p>

  <h2>Use</h2>
  <p>
    Use OSuite only for lawful business. Do not copy, resell, reverse engineer or try to bypass the licence, except where the law allows.
  </p>

  <h2>Support and changes</h2>
  <p>
    We provide support by email<span data-biz-if="phone" hidden={!b.phone}> and phone</span> during <Biz k="supportHours" fallback="working hours" />.
    We improve OSuite over time; updates are included in your plan.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    OSuite is provided with care but without a promise that it is free of every error. To the extent the law allows, our total liability for any
    claim is limited to the amount you paid us in the twelve months before it, and we are not liable for indirect losses such as lost profit or
    data you did not back up.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop at any time; see the refund policy. We may suspend a licence that is used in breach of these terms, after telling you why.
  </p>

  <h2>Law and disputes</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India. Disputes are subject to the courts of <Biz k="city" fallback="our registered city" />.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <Biz k="legalName" fallback="OfinIT" />, <Biz k="street" /> <Biz k="city" /> <Biz k="pincode" />. Email <Biz k="supportEmail" link="mailto" />.
  </p>
</Prose>
